This function tests for all pairwise interaction contrasts in a J-by-K factorial design
with independent groups using rank-based methods. The Patel-Hoel definition of interaction
states that there is no interaction if:
delta(j,jj,k,kk) = P(X_jk < X_jkk) - P(X_jjk < X_jjkk) = 0
for all pairs of levels (j,jj) of Factor A and (k,kk) of Factor B.

